### Implement supports_filters_pushdown in Rust

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/docs/source/library-user-guide/custom-table-providers.md

This method informs DataFusion which filters the provider can handle. It returns a vector of TableProviderFilterPushDown variants corresponding to each input filter.

```rust
fn supports_filters_pushdown(
    &self,
    filters: &[&Expr],
) -> Result<Vec<TableProviderFilterPushDown>> {
    Ok(filters.iter().map(|f| {
        match f {
            // We can fully evaluate equality filters on
            // the partition column at the source
            Expr::BinaryExpr(BinaryExpr {
                left, op: Operator::Eq, right
            }) if is_partition_column(left) || is_partition_column(right) => {
                TableProviderFilterPushDown::Exact
            }
            // All other filters: let DataFusion handle them
            _ => TableProviderFilterPushDown::Unsupported,
        }
    }).collect())
}
```

